WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.902
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:05.038
Thank you for being here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:06.973
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:08.341
Well, guys, this is big.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:11.043
Today, President Biden
gave U.S. intelligence agencies

00:00:11.043 --> 00:00:15.615
90 days to find out exactly
how COVID started.

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:18.718
Yep. Biden was like, "If you can
find a fiancé in 90 days,

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:19.919
you can find the truth
about COVID."

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:22.855
[ Laughter ]
"I believe that."

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:24.457
It's worth a shot. I mean,
if we've learned anything

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:25.658
from Marvel movies,

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:27.793
everyone loves
a good origin story, you know?

00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:29.562
[ Laughter ]
And I'm excited,

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.431
'cause they've already cast
Timothée Chalamet

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:33.399
to play young COVID.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:35.701
So that's gonna be cool.

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:38.604
Yep, Biden wants
the COVID origin story now.

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:41.975
Then, in 10 years, he wants
a COVID reunion on HBO Max.

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:44.643
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.643 --> 00:00:46.846
I'm pretty sure this will end
with us tracing COVID

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:49.215
back to the same lab
that came up with the McRib.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:52.118
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:53.185
I love this.

00:00:53.185 --> 00:00:55.287
It's in the shape of a rib,
isn't it?

00:00:55.287 --> 00:00:57.923
-Ribbish.
-Ribbish, right?

00:00:57.923 --> 00:00:59.959
Like, bone-in?
-Eh, no.

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:02.629
It looks like a bone-in rib.
-Like, it looks like the thing

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:04.263
that flipped over
Fred Flintstone's car.

00:01:04.263 --> 00:01:06.165
-Exactly.
That big, like a bronto-rib.

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:08.634
-I love it.
Here's some more big news.

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:11.337
Last night, it came out that a
grand jury is hearing evidence

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:14.507
against former President Trump
and could indict him.

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:15.875
-Ooh.
-Yep.

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:18.077
Trump knew he was in trouble
when he called his lawyer

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:20.246
and the FBI
answered Rudy's phone.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:23.283
[ Laughter ]
"You're being recorded."

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.552
We know a trial is close
when the courtroom sketch artist

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:26.853
goes to Michael's and says,

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.387
"Give me all the orange crayons
you have."

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:32.024
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:32.024 --> 00:01:35.228
"It's going down.
It's going down."

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:36.662
[ Applause ]

00:01:36.662 --> 00:01:38.397
Of course,
Trump responded to the news

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:39.732
in his official statement.

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:42.401
He said,
"It's a total witch hunt."

00:01:42.401 --> 00:01:44.804
Then he added,
"I'm completely innocent."

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.005
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:47.507
And finally, he said,
"Now if you'll excuse me,

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:48.808
I have to catch a flight
to Mexico."

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:50.743
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:53.946
He's innocent.

00:01:53.946 --> 00:01:56.049
Some news from the U.K.
Apparently, at the start

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:58.918
of the pandemic, British
Prime Minister Boris Johnson

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:02.755
wanted to be injected with COVID
on live TV

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:05.258
so people could see there's
nothing to be scared of.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.160
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.328
Once again, no good idea
has ever started with,

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:13.565
"I'm gonna inject myself."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.565 --> 00:02:15.902
Boris was like,
"In hindsight, it was stupid."

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.337
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:19.539
And then opened a Starbucks
bathroom door with his mouth.

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:24.144
"Aaaah!"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:26.178
Well, guys,
as we head into summer,

00:02:26.178 --> 00:02:29.515
I read that there's already
a big shortage of fireworks.

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:31.584
-Ooh.
-That's not good,

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.886
'cause the only thing worse
than mixing booze and fireworks

00:02:33.886 --> 00:02:35.954
is mixing booze
and bootleg fireworks.

00:02:35.954 --> 00:02:37.090
That's what I say.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.224
"I don't know
what the heck it does.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:40.893
Just light it."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:42.795
"Don't go near it!"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:44.530
"All right.
One selfie -- that's it.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.532
Then don't touch it!

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:47.900
Oh, look,
the dog's playing with it.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:49.101
Oh, that's fun."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.101 --> 00:02:51.770
"All right.
Take it out of his mouth."

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:53.706
Some guys are gonna be like,
"Well, I guess we could just

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:55.708
deep-fry a turkey
and hope for the worst."

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:57.777
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.777 --> 00:03:00.012
Listen to this.
In Virginia, a man created

00:03:00.012 --> 00:03:02.448
a COVID-safe way
for people to --

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:03.949
I love inventions.
-Yeah.

00:03:03.949 --> 00:03:05.651
-I love inventions.
-You do.

00:03:05.651 --> 00:03:07.119
-They're my favorite.
I really do.

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:10.556
So, this man in Virginia
created a COVID-safe way

00:03:10.556 --> 00:03:12.925
for people to blow out
birthday candles

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:16.029
by inventing a device
that's called the Blowzee.

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:19.031
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:20.833
I think it's a good idea,
but I'm not sure I want the word

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.169
Blowzee showing up
on my credit-card statement.

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:26.305
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.305 --> 00:03:29.509
And get this -- I read that over
$1 million worth of cocaine

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:33.445
tied to life jackets
washed up on a beach in England.

00:03:33.445 --> 00:03:35.647
Police got to work on the case
while the SyFy Channel

00:03:35.647 --> 00:03:37.449
got to work on "Cocaine Shark."

00:03:37.449 --> 00:03:41.954
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:41.954 --> 00:03:43.722
I'd watch --
I'd watch "Cocaine Shark."

00:03:43.722 --> 00:03:47.460
-Yeah.
-Finally, new research estimates

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:53.599
that the oldest maximum age
humans can live is 150 years.

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:55.868
Right now, there's a
149-year-old who's like,

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.603
"I thought I'd have more time."

00:03:57.603 --> 00:03:59.505
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:01.306
Guys, a lot of people
are talking about

00:04:01.306 --> 00:04:05.111
President Biden's $1.7 trillion
infrastructure plan.

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:06.345
This, by the way,
is my new voice.

00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:08.181
-You like it?
I like the black shirt,

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:10.583
the black tie,
and the smokey voice.

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:12.685
-It's almost like
a new character.

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:13.986
-Yeah.
-It's a whole new me.

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:16.021
-Chip.
-Chip?

00:04:16.021 --> 00:04:18.257
[ Laughter ]
No, no, no.

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:20.093
I think his name is, like, Jack.
-Jack or Jake.

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:23.463
-Jack Fallon.
Jake Fallon?

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:25.431
Is this a Jake Fallon or Jack?
-Jake.

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:27.566
-I think it's Jake.
-Jake.

00:04:27.566 --> 00:04:29.135
-Jake?
-Jake.

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:30.436
-Ya-ksh!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:33.072
-Jake!
-After every joke...

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:34.273
-Wa-ksh!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:35.374
Yeah.

00:04:35.374 --> 00:04:37.843
-I don't know
if it's a bluesy thing.

00:04:37.843 --> 00:04:41.013
It's more like
techno streets of Tokyo.

00:04:41.013 --> 00:04:42.148
-Right.
Like you're going --

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:44.416
You're futuristic.
-Yeah. It's raining out.

00:04:44.416 --> 00:04:46.252
-Right, like "Blade Runner."
-It's raining out.

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:47.887
There's a bunch of neon.
-Right.

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:49.822
[ Up-tempo music plays ]

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:51.824
[ Cheering ]

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:54.860
♪♪

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.629
"Come on! I've got
to get you out of here!"

00:04:56.629 --> 00:05:00.800
♪♪

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:04.370
-Jake Fallon!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.205
-Sorry.
I lost my voice the other night,

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:08.107
so now --
'Cause I was singing with --

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:10.009
When you have a sing-along with
Dave Grohl, that's what happens.

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:11.677
-What a better way
to lose your voice.

00:05:11.677 --> 00:05:13.713
-It's the best way
to lose your voice.

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:14.947
Anyways --
-I was yelling at my kids,

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:16.749
and I lost my voice.
That's not fun.

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:18.251
"Get out of here!
Get off my lawn!"

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:20.119
-That's not a charming story.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:21.987
-They weren't my kids.
They were somebody else's kids.

00:05:21.987 --> 00:05:23.255
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:23.255 --> 00:05:24.890
And you call them your kids.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:27.393
Well, the neighborhood kids.
You know.

